__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PRIVACY_POLICY_MARKDOWN_EN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ACCOUNT_DELETION_MARKDOWN_EN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const n="# Privacy Policy\n\n**SpinBook**\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how **luka4** (\u201cwe,\u201d \u201cus,\u201d or \u201cour\u201d) handles information when you use the **SpinBook** mobile application (the \u201cApp\u201d).\n\nBy using the App, you agree to this Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the App.\n\n**Last updated:** March 28, 2026\n\n---\n\n## 1. What the App does\n\nSpinBook helps you log table-tennis gear (rubbers, rackets) and activities (training and matches). Depending on how you use the App, data may stay only on your device or may be **synced to our online service** when you create an account.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Information we process\n\n**If you use the App without signing in**  \nWe do not require an account for basic local use. Your diary and inventory data are stored on your device. We do not receive that information unless you later sign in and choose to sync.\n\n**If you create an account (e.g. sign in with email)**  \nTo provide an account and sync, we process:\n\n- **Account details:** such as email address and login credentials (handled securely by our authentication provider).\n- **Profile you choose to provide:** for example display name, username, hand preference, typical rubber types, and similar profile fields you enter in the App.\n- **App content you sync:** items you choose to store in the cloud, such as rubbers, rackets, players or contacts in your diary, match and training entries, scores, dates, and related notes or labels you add.\n- **Social / friends features:** if you use friend connections, invites, inbox, or sharing sessions with friends, we process the data needed for those features (for example friend relationships, pending requests, and shared session offers or imports between accounts).\n\nWe do not use this information for advertising and we do not sell your personal information.\n\n---\n\n## 3. How we use your information\n\nWe use the information above to:\n\n- Operate the App and your account  \n- Sync your data across your devices when you are signed in  \n- Provide social features you choose to use (friends, invites, shared activities)  \n- Keep the service secure and fix problems  \n- Respond to you if you contact us  \n\nWe do not use your data for targeted ads in the App.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Where data is stored & service providers\n\nWhen you sign in and sync, your data is stored on **secure servers** operated for us by a **trusted infrastructure provider** (cloud hosting and database). That provider processes data **only on our instructions**, to run the App\u2014we do not allow them to use your personal data for their own marketing.\n\nData may be processed in countries where that provider operates facilities, subject to appropriate safeguards as required by law.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sharing with others\n\n- **Other users:** Only what the App is designed to show is visible to others\u2014for example profile fields needed for friends and usernames, or session details you explicitly share or import with a friend through the App\u2019s features. We do not make your full diary public.\n- **Legal & safety:** We may disclose information if required by law, or to protect rights, safety, and integrity of users and the service.\n- **Business transfers:** If we are involved in a merger or asset sale, your information may transfer as part of that transaction; we will require the new owner to honor this Policy or notify you of changes.\n\nWe do **not** sell your personal information.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Analytics, ads, and tracking\n\nThe App is **not** an ad-supported product. We do **not** use third-party advertising SDKs. We do **not** use analytics services that track you across other apps or websites for marketing. We may use limited technical logs on our servers (for example security or error diagnostics) in a way that does not identify you for marketing.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Optional sharing from your device\n\nFeatures such as **sharing a text summary** of your setup use your **device\u2019s built-in share sheet**. We do not control which app you send that text to or who receives it; that is your choice on your device.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Retention & your choices\n\n- **While your account exists:** we keep your account and synced data so the App works as intended.\n- **Deletion:** you can use in-App account deletion (where available) to remove your cloud account and associated data, subject to short backup or legal retention periods if required.\n- **Local data:** uninstalling the App or clearing app data on your device removes local copies on that device; **cloud data** remains until you delete your account or we delete it in line with this Policy.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Security\n\nWe use industry-standard measures (including encryption in transit) to protect your information. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure; we strive to protect your data but cannot guarantee absolute security.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Children\n\nThe App is not directed at children under 13 (or the age required in your country). We do not knowingly collect personal information from young children. If you believe we have, please contact us and we will delete it promptly.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Your rights\n\nDepending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or export your data, or to object to certain processing. Contact us using the email below and we will respond in line with applicable law.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Users in the European Economic Area and United Kingdom\n\nIf you are in the **EEA**, **UK**, or **Switzerland**, privacy rules such as the **GDPR** and **UK GDPR** give you extra protections. In plain terms:\n\n- We process your personal data to **perform our agreement with you** (running your account, sync, and the friend features you use). Sometimes we rely on **legitimate interests** that are not overridden by your rights\u2014for example keeping accounts secure and fixing abuse. Where the law requires **consent** (for certain optional processing), we will ask for it separately; you may withdraw consent at any time without affecting processing that was lawful before withdrawal.\n- You may **ask what we hold**, **correct mistakes**, **request deletion**, **limit how we use** your data in some cases, **object** to certain processing, and **receive a copy** of data you provided (**portability**), where applicable.\n- You may **complain** to your local data protection authority; in the UK this is the **ICO** ([ico.org.uk](https://ico.org.uk)). We still encourage you to contact us first so we can help.\n- If personal data is sent to countries outside the EEA/UK, we use safeguards recognised under applicable law (such as **standard contractual clauses** approved by the European Commission or UK authorities), where required.\n\nTo exercise any of these rights, email us at **luka4dev@gmail.com**.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Changes to this Policy\n\nWe may update this Policy from time to time. We will post the new \u201cLast updated\u201d date at the top. If changes are material, we may notify you in the App or by email where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Contact\n\n**luka4**  \nEmail: **luka4dev@gmail.com**\n",o="# SpinBook - Account & Data Deletion Request\n\nSpinBook (by luka4) lets you request deletion of your account and associated cloud data.\n\n## How to request deletion\n1. Send an email to **luka4dev@gmail.com**\n2. Use the **same email address** that you use to sign in to SpinBook (e.g.: the Google account email).\n3. Use the subject: **SpinBook \u2014 Delete my account**\n4. In the email body, include:\n   - Your **SpinBook username**\n   - The Google account **email address** used in the app\n   - A clear statement that you want your account deleted\n\nExample:\n\nSubject: SpinBook \u2014 Delete my account\n\nHello,  \nPlease delete my SpinBook account and associated data.  \nUsername: peter22  \nAccount email: peter22@example.com\n\nThank you.\n\n## What will be deleted\nWhen your request is verified, we delete the cloud data associated with your SpinBook account, which may include:\n- Your profile (username, display name, avatar)\n- Your friends / social connections and inbox items\n- Your synced diary entries (training/matches), notes, and related metadata\n- Your synced inventory (rubbers, blades, rackets)\n- Any photos you uploaded for activities and your profile avatar (stored in cloud storage)\n\n## What may be kept\n- Emails you send to support may be retained for support/legal purposes.\n\n## Important note about shared activities\nIf you shared an activity with a friend, they receive a separate copy of that activity.\nWhen your account is deleted, your friend\u2019s copy remains in their account and is not deleted automatically.\n\n## Retention period\nDeletion requests are typically processed within **[10 business days]**.  \nIf a longer retention period is required (for legal/security reasons), we will inform you by email.\n\n## Important note\nIf you used SpinBook in guest/offline mode only (no sign-in), your data is stored on your device and can be removed by uninstalling the app."},1436,[]);
